    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1190">

                <pb facs="1191" n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8460</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Fletcher to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 221</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegram No. 217, May 31, 7 p.m., I have the honor to state that a communication
                    has been received from the Foreign Office to the effect that the matter had been
                    referred to the War Department with the recommendation that orders be issued to
                    afford adequate protection to the lives and interests of American citizens in
                    the Yaqui Valley.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
